    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0594" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60 p 31/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Coleman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-23T14:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                                1925—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 23—10:49
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>96. My telegram number 95, November 17, 4 p.m., also despatch number 3262,
                    October 10th.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d314-f1"/> Has Department any objection to
                    including Finland among list of countries excluded from operation provisional
                    trade agreement? If no objection, I assume I still have authority to sign text
                    submitted by Department in telegram 42, August 23, 2 p.m., 1924, and number 39,
                    August 4, 3 p.m., this year. I am advised agreement is likely now and to be
                    signed here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Coleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
